and after his  polemic towards philosophers he goes on  addressing a plethora of topics like the  notion of the free spirit the natural  history of morals and analysis of people  and countries of his time as well as his  examination of the essence of nobility  it is important to note that nietzsche  considered a lot of his views as an  experiment in abstract reasoning he is  someone whose methodology is deeply  entangled in what could be called  what-if scenarios as it is stated in the  introduction of the cambridge edition of  the book we find embedded in nietzsche's  basic view of himself the recommendation  not that we read his texts as aiming at  objectively valid judgments adjustments  that are true irrespective of the  cultural and psychological context in  which they are made but that we think of  them as narratives that he invites us to  listen to without really obliging us to  believe in them reading nietzsche  requires an open mind we expect a lot  from philosophers but we also need to  see nietzsche's works as a fusion of  philosophy poetry and masterfully  articulated abstract reasoning he was a  pioneer of thought and regardless of the  errors spotted in some of his thinking  motifs he still revolutionized the way  we think and we should all be grateful  for this  it is the business of the very few to be  independent it is the privilege of the  strong and whoever attempts it even with  the best right but without being obliged  to do so proves that he is probably not  only strong but also daring beyond  measure he enters into a labyrinth he  multiplies a thousand-fold the dangers  which life in itself already brings with  it not the list of which says that not  one can see how and where he loses his  way becomes isolated and his torn  piecemeal by some minotaur of conscience  supposing such a one comes to grief it  is so far from the comprehension of men  that they neither feel it nor sympathize  with it and he cannot any longer go back  he cannot even go back again to the  sympathy of men  owning oneself is not an easy task  nietzsche looks at the world around him  and sees mainly people who prefer to be  dependent rather than independent this  annoyed him a lot and to the degree that  he adopted more or less an elitist  stance towards others and this becomes  more apparent in his idea about slave  and master morality as this will be  discussed in a bit nietzsche believed  that it's in our passions where we find  ourselves this belief constituted one of  his main attempts to use philosophy as  an instrument to understand and engage  with the human psyche throughout the  enlightenment reason was the predominant  virtue essentially most philosophers  espoused the view that through reason a  person becomes enlightened nietzsche  however opposed this idea as quite  conservative he believed that reason the  way it was portrayed during his time was  equated with conservatism and  suppression of our nature he does not  want us to suppress our instincts our  passions our emotions but to confront  them and embrace them that is how we  understand ourselves better that is how  we own ourselves  without a deep understanding of the  nature of our inner world we are just  constantly exposed to a fake reality and  become victims to the twists and turns  of life we must constantly test  ourselves as he writes one must subject  oneself to one's own tests that one is  destined for independence and command  and do so at the right time one must not  avoid one's tests although they  constitute perhaps the most dangerous  game one can play and are in the end  tests made only before ourselves and  before no other judge  how could anything originate out of its  opposite for example truth out of error  or the will to truth out of the will to  deception or the generous deed out of  selfishness in spite of all the value  which may be longer to the true the  positive and the unselfish it might be  possible that a higher and more  fundamental value for life generally  should be assigned to pretense to the  will to delusion to selfishness and  cupidity it might even be possible that  what constitutes the value of those good  and respected things consists precisely  in their being insidiously related noted  and crocheted to this evil and  apparently opposed things perhaps even  in being essentially identical with them  perhaps but who wishes to concern  himself with such dangerous perhapses  reading nietzsche can be frustrating at  times as a person who is strongly  defending his positions one would  imagine that he is an evangelist of  truth but why is he so adamantly  promulgating the opposite of that in the  previous passage in another passage he  writes the strength of a person's spirit  would then be measured by how much truth  he could tolerate or more precisely to  what extent he needs to have it diluted  disguised sweetened muted falsified the  contradiction is quite evident or is it  i guess that every great thinker needs  to battle with this kind of  contradictions truth can be difficult to  define at times truth can be nuanced it  can be multifaceted it can be  complicated our willingness to pursue it  constitutes a very onerous endeavor and  our ability to tolerate truth showcases  the strength of our character granted  that we want the truth why not rather  untruth and uncertainty even ignorance  the problem of the value of truth  presented itself before us or was it we  who presented ourselves before the  problem the idea of questioning almost  everything is emblematic of nietzsche's  writing style through this process he  recognizes that one becomes smarter and  cultivates a more holistic understanding  of the world more specifically he likes  to go against the dogmatic nature of  philosophical prejudices so he urges us  to question our assumptions and our  dogmatic beliefs especially when we  philosophize as i said before nietzsche  wrote this book during a time when  psychology and science were at an  embryonic stage he was sensing that we  will be in a position very soon to  understand the world around us better so  it is time to destroy the old world and  lay the groundwork for the new one  in a tour through the many finer and  coarser moralities which have hitherto  prevailed or still prevail on the earth  i found certain traits recurring  regularly together and connected with  one another until finally two primary  types revealed themselves to me and the  radical distinction was brought to light  there is master morality and slave  morality nietzsche touches upon the  concept of master versus slave morality  in beyond good and evil  and expands on it in the genealogy of  morality before i attempt an analysis of  the concept i want to point out that i'm  not in favor of the use of the words  master and slave here nietzsche believes  in self-responsibility so he considers  hierarchies a natural byproduct of our  nature the ones who are strong and  responsible will rise to the top of the  hierarchy and the ones who aren't will  stay at the bottom for me such  distinctions are just by-products of our  social mythology i am against  hierarchies and against anything that  creates inequality and polarization  within our social systems regardless  nietzsche tries to make a point here the  point is that a person who adheres to a  master morality is a person with a  heroic attitude he alludes to the  ancient greek heroes as archetypes of  this kind of morality master morality is  the morality of the strong willed its  essence is to focus on everything that  is noble qualities that are often valued  in master morality are open-mindedness  courage truthfulness trustworthiness and  inaccurate sense of self-worth on the  other hand slave morality is the  morality of the weak-minded as it is  eloquently stated in wikipedia slave  morality does not aim at exerting one's  will by strength but by careful  subversion nietzsche believes that  people who adhere to slave morality seek  equality just because they don't want to  work on themselves and instead of trying  to become masters they prefer to bring  everyone to their own level again i  believe that this is a critique to  everything that is weak similar to  seneca's critique when he wrote that all  cruelty springs from weakness the slave  and master morality can be competing  forces within one's psyche as he writes  i would at once add however that in all  higher and mixed civilizations there are  also attempts at the reconciliation of  the two moralities but one still finds  off an error the confusion and mutual  misunderstanding of them indeed  sometimes their close juxtaposition even  in the same man within one soul  nietzsche didn't propose the master  slave morality dichotomy as a panacea to  our moral conundrums he believed that a  constant re-evaluation of our moral  landscape could give us a better  understanding of our inner world as i  said before these are not the most ideal  terms to use when covering such  sensitive topics but nietzsche always  wanted to make noise and would use  controversial terms in order to be heard  in any case while aiming towards a  philosophy of the future one must always  have in mind that equality cannot exist  without self-responsibility  hey guys hope you enjoyed today's video  if you did make sure to like subscribe  turn on notifications and comment below  something cool please so that more  people can discover it  if you want to watch more videos from my  channel check out this one and this one  take care see you soon editor now  you
 

